Speech model weights downloaded on demand by Speedwave's meeting-transcription
feature. These files are NOT bundled in the installer — they are fetched (with
SHA-256 verification) from the upstream host listed below the first time they
are needed, and stored under `~/.speedwave/models/`.

--- Whisper speech-to-text weights (ggml format) ---

OpenAI Whisper model weights, repackaged in whisper.cpp's `ggml` format.

Upstream: https://huggingface.co/ggerganov/whisper.cpp
Original model: https://github.com/openai/whisper
License: MIT (OpenAI's Whisper models are released under the MIT license; the
ggml repackaging adds no additional restrictions).

--- Silero VAD voice-activity weights (ggml format) ---

Silero VAD v5.1.2, converted to whisper.cpp's `ggml` format, used to skip
silence before transcription.

Upstream: https://huggingface.co/ggml-org/whisper-vad
Original model: https://github.com/snakers4/silero-vad
License: MIT (Copyright (c) 2020-present Silero Team).

--- Nemotron-3 Diarization weights (GGUF format) ---

NVIDIA Nemotron-3 Diarization, q8_0 GGUF, used only when the user turns on
"Tell speakers apart in the meeting audio" in Settings.

Upstream: https://huggingface.co/nvidia/Nemotron-3-Diarization
License: OpenMDW-1.1, https://openmdw.ai/license/1-1/

Speedwave only downloads and runs these weights locally; it does not
redistribute them. If you redistribute a copy of `~/.speedwave/models/`, the
above licenses apply to the respective files.
